---
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "@fancyapps/ui/dist/fancybox/fancybox.css";
import AnimatedLink from "../components/AnimatedLink.astro";
import BodyText from "../components/BodyText.astro";
import Cell from "../components/Cell.astro";
import Greetings from "../components/Greetings.astro";
import Grid from "../components/Grid.astro";
import ImageCell from "../components/ImageCell.astro";
import Logo from "../components/Logo.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <Header>
    <Logo />
    <Nav />
    <Greetings greeting="Photos and other visual ventures" />
  </Header>

  <main class="page-content">
    <Grid>
      <Cell width={3}>
        <h4>Selected works</h4>
        <BodyText>
          Here is a small selection of my favorite pictures. Mostly, my interest
          in photography has been shapes and textures, and how they interact.
          Recently, I've embraced black and white, as I find it really lets those
          elements shine. The best way to get an idea of the kind of
          photography I do is to simply have a look around. The photos will speak
          for themselves.
        </BodyText>

        <BodyText>
          I also sell prints, and I plan to add a shop here eventually. Until
          then, if you're interested in a print, or if you'd like to use one of
          these photos, just send me a message on <AnimatedLink
            href="https://www.instagram.com/guillaume_tech/"
            >Instagram</AnimatedLink
          >.
        </BodyText>
      </Cell>
      <ImageCell
        imageName="sapin.jpg"
        alt="A small pine tree covered in snow and decorated with Christmas baubles against a white winter backdrop."
        loading="eager"
        spanV={2}
      />

      <ImageCell
        imageName="course.jpg"
        alt="A person running past a vibrant installation of colorful vertical poles."
        loading="eager"
        spanV={2}
        spanH={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="industrie.jpg"
        alt="A black and white view of an industrial tower seen behind a fence."
        loading="eager"
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="pont.jpg"
        alt="An elevated view of a winding bike path along a riverbank near a tall power line tower."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="stlau.jpg"
        alt="A bare tree on a snowy riverbank during a hazy winter snowfall."
        loading="eager"
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="verdun.jpg"
        alt="A car covered with a tarp in a residential back alley with outdoor spiral staircases."
        loading="eager"
      />

      <ImageCell
        imageName="car.jpg"
        alt="A classic vintage convertible car driving along a port harbor with a large cruise ship docked in the background."
        loading="lazy"
      />

      <ImageCell
        imageName="cirque.jpg"
        alt="A multiple-exposure photo of acrobats performing with glowing hoops on a dark stage."
        loading="lazy"
      />

      <ImageCell
        imageName="yatch.jpg"
        alt="A view through rocky cliff formations looking down onto a harbor filled with yachts."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="ottawa.jpg"
        alt="A black and white architectural shot highlighting the geometric windows of brutalist concrete buildings."
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <Cell height={1}>
        <h4>Gear</h4>
        <BodyText>
          I don't think gear matters that much, but if you're interested: I mostly
          shoot at 35 mm or 50 mm. For film photography, I use a Spotmatic F, and
          for digital, I use either a Sony a6000 or a Fujifilm X100VI.
        </BodyText>
      </Cell>
      <ImageCell
        imageName="plage.jpg"
        alt="People relaxing under beach umbrellas on a pebbly riverbank with stone bridges in the background."
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="ville-marie.jpg"
        alt="A low-angle black and white photograph of a tall skyscraper disappearing into thick fog."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="creuse.jpg"
        alt="A peaceful French village nestled along the edge of a calm lake surrounded by trees."
        loading="lazy"
        spanH={2}
        spanV={2}
      />

      <ImageCell
        imageName="barn.jpg"
        alt="An abandoned vintage yellow sports car partially overgrown by wild berry bushes and grass."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="avion.jpg"
        alt="A black and white photograph of an airplane cabin with light streaming through the windows."
        loading="lazy"
        spanH={2}
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="building.jpg"
        alt="A black and white architectural photo of modern geometric concrete structures with circular cutouts."
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="nyc1.jpg"
        alt="A vibrant night street view of New York City surrounded by glowing neon billboards and illuminated storefronts."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="nyc3.jpg"
        alt="A cozy outdoor café patio at night illuminated by string lights with patrons sitting at tables."
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="nyc2.jpg"
        alt="A view of Manhattan skyscrapers including One World Trade Center rising above surrounding city buildings."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="tremblant.jpg"
        alt="A landscape view of forested mountains stretching towards a distant lake in the haze."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="oregon.jpg"
        alt="A black and white upward view looking through tall, misty pine tree canopies."
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </Grid>

    <Grid>
      <Cell width={2}>
        <h4>Other media</h4>
        <BodyText>
          While photography is a big part of my creative output, I'm fascinated
          by creating images. Besides photography, I've made posters for dozens
          of events and experimented with Photoshop, Blender, and other tools.
          More recently, I've developed an interest in traditional media and
          tried my hand at linocutting. The following is a small excerpt; I'll add
          more later.
        </BodyText>
      </Cell>
      <ImageCell
        imageName="bg2.png"
        alt="A black-and-white render of an abstract tube-like shape tied in a knot."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="bg.png"
        alt="A purple-and-gold render of an abstract tube-like shape tied in a knot."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
        spanH={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="island.jpg"
        alt="A render of a group of islands with a sailboat and a small visible campsite."
        loading="lazy"
        spanV={2}
      />
      <ImageCell
        imageName="phare.jpg"
        alt="A 3D render of a lighthouse in the mist."
        loading="lazy"
        spanH={2}
        spanV={2}
      />
    </Grid>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  import { Fancybox } from "@fancyapps/ui/dist/fancybox/";

  Fancybox.bind("[data-fancybox]", {
    theme: "auto",
    mainStyle: {
      "--f-button-width": "44px",
      "--f-button-height": "44px",
      "--f-toolbar-padding": "16px",
    },
    Carousel: {
      Arrows: false,
      Toolbar: {
        display: {
          left: [],
          middle: [],
          right: ["close"],
        },
      },
    },
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* astro-lqip: keep the blurry overlay ON TOP of the img while it streams in.
	   The img has z-index:1; the ::after starts at --z-index (0 by default).
	   Setting it to 2 means the placeholder covers the partially-decoded image.
	   Once onload fires, astro-lqip resets --z-index to 1 and --opacity to 0. */
  :global([data-astro-lqip]) {
    --z-index: 2;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  :global([data-astro-lqip]::after) {
    filter: blur(10px);
    transform: scale(1.2);
  }
</style>
